     1	"""Primitive V0.25 worlds backed by the read-only legacy scenario stack.
     2	
     3	The binding deliberately has only one interpretation of a physical beam:
     4	``(NORAD, cell_id)``.  ``cell_id`` is the legacy earth-fixed hex-cell index;
     5	its reuse colour is ``CellGrid.colors[cell_id]``.  Thus a beam identity is
     6	stable when action slots or a user's seven-cell neighbourhood are re-keyed.
     7	
     8	An episode start is drawn exactly as in the C3-S screen: a world seed is
     9	expanded by ``SeedSequence.spawn(4)``, child zero draws a TRAIN epoch and
    10	child one scatters/moves the 100 users.  Element sets are selected once at
    11	that epoch.  For each NORAD the closest epoch in the available files at
    12	date-1/date/date+1 is retained, subject to the legacy 24-hour age ceiling;
    13	the selected TLE is then propagated for the whole tape (it is not reselected
    14	at each boundary).
    15	
    16	The legacy D2/TTT history uses 47 samples spanning 46 measurement intervals
    17	backward and ending at each decision instant.  V0.25 integration instead
    18	uses 48 boundaries spanning 47 intervals forward from that instant.  The
    19	provider takes boundary-zero eligibility from the legacy backward history,
    20	then advances it only for k=1..47; no forward sample can admit a candidate at
    21	the decision instant.
    22	
    23	Engine boundaries are immutable NumPy arrays.  Python candidate objects are
    24	created only by the audit view.  No environment, ``SatelliteSet``, sgp4
    25	``Satrec``, or process-global world cache crosses the primitive seam.
    26	"""
